<title>GREECE: BANK OF CYPRUS CUTS LOAN, DEPOSIT RATES.</title>
<headline>BANK OF CYPRUS CUTS LOAN, DEPOSIT RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Cyprus joined other</p>
<p>banks with cuts in its loan and savings deposit rates, it said</p>
<p>in a statement.</p>
<p>Its new rate structure has as follows:</p>
<p>    Base loan rate:	     17.25 percent</p>
<p>    Consumer loans:	     22.75 percent</p>
<p>    Housing loans:		15.75 percent</p>
<p>    Construction loans	  20.75 percent</p>
<p>Its deposit reates will be the following:</p>
<p>    Savings deposit rate:     11.00 percent</p>
<p>    CYPLUS deposit account:   up to 12 percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
